[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Van Geet Opening"]
[Variation "Van Geet Opening: Anglo-Scandinavian"]
[ECO "A00"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "space,closed-centre"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "1.Nc3"]

1. Nc3 d5 { Takes the centre. A knight on c3 blocks White's own c-pawn, so Black can claim space. } 2. e4 ( 2. d4 Nf6 3. Bf4 a6 { Takes the b5 square away from the knight. From b5 it would jump to c7 and fork the king and rook. } 4. e3 e6 5. Nf3 c5 ) ( 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. d4 e6 4. Bg5 Be7 { The pin on the f6 knight is harmless once the bishop is on e7. } ) 2... d4 { Gains space with tempo: the c3 knight has to move and has few good squares. } 3. Nce2 e5 { Props up d4 and closes the centre, so White's lead in development counts for little. } 4. Ng3 Nf6 { Attacks e4, so White has to look after it. } 5. Bc4 c5 { A second pawn behind d4. Plan: ...Nc6, ...Bd6 and ...O-O; with the centre closed there is no rush. } 6. d3 Nc6 *
